The theorem deliberately does not assert a unique full message profile. Strongly convex primal objectives do not ensure unique multipliers. For example, a strongly concave valuation kink at a binding allocation can support an interval of common prices. Even smooth valuations with active local bounds can have nonunique coupling multipliers. A separate multiplier-uniqueness assumption would give full NE uniqueness.
